## Flash Loan Vulnerability in EVault

## Context
*File*: Borrowing.sol#L65-L78

## Description
The `EVault` provides a flash loan function that allows any user to borrow the underlying asset as long as they repay it within the same transaction. The flash loan function can be disabled, or users may be required to pay a certain percentage of the flash loan as a fee in advance, depending on the hook configurations of the `EVault`. 

Additionally, `EVault` allows any user to borrow the underlying asset as long as they provide sufficient collateral. However, it only checks if the borrower has enough collateral at the end of the call due to the checks deferral feature of EVC. 

Since `EVault` supports batch calls, any user can exploit this feature to borrow the underlying asset from any `EVault` and repay it within the same transaction without incurring any fees, thereby effectively bypassing the flash loan restrictions of the `EVault`:

- The borrower doesn't need to provide any collateral.
- Anyone can do this even if the flash loan feature is disabled.
- The borrower doesn't need to pay any fees, resulting in the `EVault` losing flash loan fees.

