## Context
The function `validateFlashloan` in `ValidationLogic` is used to validate the parameters of flashloans executed by a user. One of the new checks introduced in AAVE 3.1 adds an extra soft protection on borrowing actions, expecting the transaction to revert if the amount borrowed exceeds the total supply of the respective aToken. Although this check will always hold when executing `flashLoanSimple` or `borrow`, it will not hold in the case of `flashLoan`.

